{
  "id": "flutter-disable-losing-baby-mario",
  "name": "Disable Losing Baby Mario",
  "category": "Flutter! - Death Mechanics",
  "description": "Yoshi never loses Baby Mario: the kidnap cutscene (Kamek / Bandit / Toady), the bubble float-away and re-mount, and the enemy-swallow cinematics (Wild Piranha, Spooky ghost, goal-ring and Grim-Leecher catches) are all neutralized. Normal deaths (pits, lava, spikes) still work.",
  "attribution": "Extracted from the Flutter hack (https://www.romhacking.net/hacks/8972/)",
  "details": [
    "Across the lose/kidnap/respawn/catch routines (banks 02/04/05/06) the kidnap/catch actor is despawned, made invisible, and given no hitbox, and the SuperFX cinematic status flags are never set, so the lose-Baby-Mario and swallow cinematics never engage. The enemy-swallow cleanup is bundled in on purpose: with the lose sequence disabled, a swallow would otherwise leave Baby Mario stuck. The shared death-gamemode trigger at $04:F6D1 is deliberately LEFT INTACT (Flutter NOPs it, but that breaks every death since pits/lava/spikes route through the same trigger). Extracted from the Flutter hack (https://www.romhacking.net/hacks/8972/), minus Flutter's death-gamemode suppression."
  ],
  "source": "builtin",
  "romVersionAuthored": "YI_U1",
